{{ElectionsAZ}}
The '''1982 Arizona gubernatorial election''' took place on November 2, 1982, for the post of [[List of governors of Arizona|Governor of Arizona]]. [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] incumbent [[Bruce Babbitt]] defeated [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] nominee [[Leo Corbet]] and [[Libertarian Party (United States)|Libertarian]] candidate and former [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. Representative]] [[Sam Steiger]]. [[Evan Mecham]] unsuccessfully ran for the Republican nomination.

This was the last time until [[2002 Arizona gubernatorial election|2002]] that a Democrat would be elected Governor of Arizona.{{Efn|[[Rose Mofford]], a [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democrat]], would serve as governor from 1988 to 1991 following the impeachment of [[List of governors of Arizona|Governor]] [[Evan Mecham]], but was never officially elected as Governor.}}

